--changed-since` no default (llm_eval.py:46-50), so an absent flag is `None` and a present-but-empty flag is `''` — both falsy and indistinguishable at the line-180 guard.",".github/workflows/prompt-eval.yml:85 runs `rebar criteria eval --changed-since \"$CHANGED_SINCE\" --require-live`, so an unset env var yields exactly `--changed-since \"\"`, the plan's target scenario.","As specified, updating only `_is_null_ref` leaves the exit-2 symptom unchanged: the mechanism does not achieve the plan's stated no-op goal."],"finding":"The empty-`--changed-since ''` fix targets `_is_null_ref`, but that function is never reached for an empty value: the dispatch guard routes empty/absent `--changed-since` to the exit-2 missing-criterion path before `_criteria_eval_changed_since` (which calls `_is_null_ref`) is invoked.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f575a0b46d6ed4fb6","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section 'Plan' bullet 4 ('Treat an empty --changed-since value as a null/no-baseline ref') and Root Cause ('_is_null_ref recognizes all-zero SHAs but not an explicitly empty --changed-since'); code at src/rebar/_cli/_llm_eval_commands.py:179-182, 244-251, 296-299","norm_id":"n0f9327ea5afe33cd","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["CI push event where the `before`/baseline env var is unset, producing `--changed-since \"\"`, expecting a clean no-op but getting exit 2."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Distinguish 'flag present' from 'flag absent' (e.g. parser default sentinel, or check `args.changed_since is not None`) and route a present-but-empty value into `_criteria_eval_changed_since`, where the updated `_is_null_ref` then yields the no-op; do not rely on the falsy `if args.changed_since:` guard at line 180.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the disposition the new `--require-live` zero-success failure surfaces (fatal/permanent vs retryable/transient), and whether a run where every criterion failed on a retryable LLMError preserves that retryable disposition rather than collapsing to a generic non-zero exit.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.engine-layer-enforcement","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["project.failure-disposition-contract"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.9,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'--require-live can fail when live execution was attempted but produced zero successful evaluations'","The per-criterion LLMError arm is caught-and-continued; the aggregate zero-success arm is the newly-added failure arm, but no disposition word (retryable/transient vs fatal/permanent) is attached to it."],"finding":"The plan makes `--require-live` fail non-zero when zero live criteria succeed, but does not state which disposition that failure carries when the underlying LLMErrors were retryable/transient (e.g. all criteria failed on a Bedrock 429 throttle). A blanket non-zero exit masks a retryable primary failure as an undifferentiated fatal one.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9ad20835644fffe9","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan bullet: 'Have the live selected-criteria loop return a success count so --require-live can fail when live execution was attempted but produced zero successful evaluations.'","norm_id":"nf67757cb67388a6b","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Under --require-live, all selected criteria raise a transient LLMError (throttle / temporary Bedrock 429); the run exits non-zero as a hard failure with no signal that a retry would have succeeded — a retryable condition surfaces as fatal."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"bad4e0cc7331011f","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["d141a0626afe5115",4208],"description_boxes":["7879981d4f226a8f",0],"file_impact":["7b40f88a53ae2ccc",2],"ticket_id":["824462a2d461d952",19]},"metrics":{"cache_read_tokens":728652,"cache_write_to